# Architecture Rules

## Project Structure
- Use App Router directory structure
- Keep components focused and modular
- Implement proper route grouping
- Use proper parallel routes
- Keep proper intercepting routes
- Implement proper loading states
- Use proper error boundaries
- Keep proper route handlers

## Component Architecture
- Use Server Components by default
- Add 'use client' only when necessary
- Keep components focused
- Implement proper component composition
- Use proper prop typing
- Keep proper error boundaries
- Implement proper loading states
- Use proper suspense boundaries

## Data Flow
- Use Server Actions for mutations
- Implement React Query for client state
- Use proper data fetching patterns
- Keep proper caching strategies
- Implement proper revalidation
- Use proper optimistic updates
- Keep proper error handling
- Implement proper loading states

## State Management
- Use Server Components state by default
- Implement URL state with searchParams
- Use React Query for server state
- Keep client state minimal
- Use proper form state
- Implement proper validation
- Keep proper error handling
- Use proper loading states

## Authentication
- Use Auth.js (v5) for authentication
- Implement proper session management
- Use proper middleware
- Keep proper route protection
- Implement proper role-based access
- Use proper error handling
- Keep proper loading states
- Implement proper session revalidation

## Performance
- Use proper code splitting
- Implement proper lazy loading
- Use proper caching strategies
- Keep proper bundle size
- Implement proper prefetching
- Use proper asset optimization
- Keep proper monitoring
- Implement proper error tracking

